(Solution Step 1: Volume of 0.5 N KOH Consumed:) Tj
T*
(V_consumed = V_blank - V_test = 24.5 mL - 12.0 mL = 12.5 mL of 0.5 N KOH.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Saponification Value Formula:) Tj
T*
(Saponification Value = [ V_consumed * Normality of KOH * 56.1 ] / Mass of Oil \(g\)) Tj
T*
(\(where 56.1 is molecular weight of KOH in g/mol\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculation:) Tj
T*
(Saponification Value = [ 12.5 * 0.5 * 56.1 ] / 2.50 = [ 6.25 * 56.1 ] / 2.50 = 350.625 /) Tj
T*
(2.50 = 140.25 mg KOH / g of oil.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Saponification value of 140.25 indicates significant presence of) Tj
T*
(saponifiable triglyceride/vegetable oil blended into the mineral base.) Tj
T*
