([SOLVED PROBLEM 3: Acid Number Determination of Used Oil]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: 5.00 g of used turbine oil required 3.20 mL of 0.05 N KOH solution for complete) Tj
T*
(neutralization of free fatty acids using phenolphthalein indicator. Calculate the Acid) Tj
T*
(Number and evaluate if oil replacement is required \(Replacement threshold: Acid number >) Tj
T*
(0.5 mg KOH/g\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Acid Number Formula:) Tj
T*
(Acid Number = [ V_KOH * N_KOH * 56.1 ] / Mass of Oil \(g\)) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Substitute Values:) Tj
T*
(Acid Number = [ 3.20 mL * 0.05 N * 56.1 ] / 5.00 g = [ 0.160 * 56.1 ] / 5.00 = 8.976 /) Tj
T*
(5.00 = 1.795 mg KOH / g.) Tj
T*
(Evaluation: The acid value \(1.80 mg KOH/g\) substantially exceeds the 0.5 mg KOH/g safety) Tj
T*
(limit due to oxidative rancidity and sludge formation. The oil must be replaced) Tj
T*
(immediately to prevent bearing corrosion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([SOLVED PROBLEM 4: Chemical Composition of Bogue's Compounds in Portland Cement]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A Portland cement clinker contains the following oxide percentages: CaO =) Tj
T*
(64.0%, SiO2 = 21.0%, Al2O3 = 6.0%, Fe2O3 = 3.0%. Calculate the percentage of Tricalcium) Tj
T*
(Silicate \(C3S\) and Dicalcium Silicate \(C2S\) using Bogue's empirical equations:) Tj
T*
(% C3S = 4.071 * \(% CaO\) - 7.600 * \(% SiO2\) - 6.718 * \(% Al2O3\) - 1.430 * \(% Fe2O3\).) Tj
T*
(% C2S = 2.867 * \(% SiO2\) - 0.7544 * \(% C3S\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Calculate % C3S:) Tj
T*
(% C3S = 4.071 * \(64.0\) - 7.600 * \(21.0\) - 6.718 * \(6.0\) - 1.430 * \(3.0\)) Tj
T*
(% C3S = 260.544 - 159.600 - 40.308 - 4.290 = 260.544 - 204.198 = 56.35%.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate % C2S:) Tj
T*
(% C2S = 2.867 * \(21.0\) - 0.7544 * \(56.35\) = 60.207 - 42.511 = 17.70%.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Clinker consists of 56.35% C3S \(providing rapid early strength\) and 17.70%) Tj
T*
(C2S \(providing progressive long-term hardening\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
