T*
(* Q1: Describe the three mechanisms of lubrication \(Thick film, Thin film, and) Tj
T*
(Extreme Pressure\) with appropriate operating condition diagrams.) Tj
T*
(Answer: \(1\) Hydrodynamic \(Thick-Film\) Lubrication: Operates under high speeds and) Tj
T*
(low-to-moderate loads. A continuous fluid lubricant film \(~1,000 A thick\) completely) Tj
T*
(separates opposing metal surfaces. Viscous shear resistance within the lubricant layer) Tj
T*
(replaces solid friction \(friction coefficient mu ~ 0.001 - 0.03\). \(2\) Boundary) Tj
T*
(\(Thin-Film\) Lubrication: Operates under low speeds or high loads where fluid films) Tj
T*
(cannot be maintained. Asperities come into near-contact, separated only by an adsorbed) Tj
T*
(organic monolayer. Long-chain polar molecules \(stearic acid, oleic acid\) orient) Tj
T*
(perpendicularly, their polar heads bonding electrostatically to the metal surface while) Tj
T*
(hydrocarbon tails project outward \(mu ~ 0.05 - 0.15\). \(3\) Extreme-Pressure \(EP\)) Tj
T*
(Lubrication: Operates under extreme shock loads and high localized temperatures \(>200) Tj
T*
(deg C\). Boundary monolayers thermally desorb. Organic compounds of Sulfur, Chlorine, or) Tj
T*
(Phosphorus react chemically with iron to form low-shear-strength solid inorganic layers) Tj
T*
(\(FeS, FeCl2\) preventing metal-to-metal welding and catastrophic scoring.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the setting and hardening of Portland cement, detailing the role of) Tj
T*
(gypsum and hydration reactions of Bogue's compounds.) Tj
T*
(Answer: When Portland cement is mixed with water, hydration and hydrolysis reactions) Tj
T*
(occur: \(1\) Initial Setting: Tricalcium aluminate \(C3A\) hydrates vigorously within) Tj
T*
(minutes: C3A + 6 H2O -> C3A.6H2O. This rapid reaction causes premature 'Flash Set',) Tj
T*
(locking the paste before placement. \(2\) Role of Gypsum: To prevent flash setting, 2-3%) Tj
T*
(gypsum \(CaSO4.2H2O\) is interground with clinker. Gypsum dissolves and reacts with C3A to) Tj
T*
(form an insoluble coating of calcium sulfoaluminate \(Ettringite\): C3A + 3 CaSO4.2H2O +) Tj
T*
(26 H2O -> C3A.3CaSO4.32H2O. This protective needle-like layer retards C3A hydration,) Tj
T*
(extending workability to ~45 minutes. \(3\) Hardening: Tricalcium silicate \(C3S\) hydrates) Tj
T*
(within 7 days, providing early compressive strength: 2 C3S + 6 H2O -> C3S2.3H2O) Tj
T*
(\(Tobermorite C-S-H gel\) + 3 Ca\(OH\)2. Dicalcium silicate \(C2S\) hydrates slowly over) Tj
T*
(months to years, developing progressive ultimate rock-like strength.) Tj
T*
() Tj
